king overtraining obviously I  don't recommend that the average doe do  this however it's a useful tool to have  in your arsenal for most of us we want  to climb back down we might even want to  slow down that descent because that way  we're creating lots of muscle damage and  we can build this really big biceps at  the same time like I said wrote  climbing's fantastic for work capacity  because you're constantly moving you can  do these four huge rep ranges and you're  never letting up with the tension  because you need to hold onto the Rope  at all times even in between reps using  your whole body as well and yeah the  fact that you're using a whole body it's  really evident in just how much your abs  will hurt from doing this and how much  you'll develop your core over time  because as you climb with the rope not  using your legs you can have to put them  somewhere that means you're using a  static contraction with your abs and in  order to swing your body create the  torque you need to use the movement to  climb the rope it's a full-body really  functional exercise and what's really  cool about it is it has a real world  direct application you can imagine using  rope climbs to scale a building like a  ninja or rappel down it when you're  breaking through a roof to stop some  terrorists it's just a really cool  awesome way to Train there's a lot of  fun as well which is what I really like  about it when I'm training with rope  climbs what I like to do is climb  the rope and then climb all around my  pull-up bar because it's got multiple  attachments and do things like front  levers and maybe a quick one arm to pull  up and things like that drop down onto  the rope and just really experiment with  the movement and that's a really fun way  to Train it's really varied and there's  a small element of risk and all this  means that ya really don't get bored and  I'm using that kind of training of  course this is also a fantastic way to  build up to one arm to pull up because  essentially that's what you're doing  every time you reach up the rope you're  holding your weight with one arm  before you get started though there are  a few safety considerations to bear in  mind and a few technique tips this is  really intense on your elbow tendons and  if you dive straight into high volume  rope climbs or rope crowns with some  kind of added weight then you're going  to really quickly damage your elbows and  this can put you out of action for a  long time so I recommend that you build  up that elbow that straight arm strength  before you start doing your rope crimes  you can do this with supper nated  support holds on the rings or rings  turned out push up so you can do it with  pseudo planche you can do it with  Maltese push-ups or you can do it with  the crow pose or any kind of straight  arm training like that and of course by  introducing low-volume rope climbs just  taking it easy to begin with really  build up to this carefully if you feel  any pain in your elbows stop immediately  another tip is to always keep your arms  bent don't dangle from your arm with a  straight arm because that's a very quick  way to injure yourself at the same time  you should try and have your hands at  about face level when you cross over and  twist your grip inwards when you hold on  to the rope this will not only allow you  to get harder and reduce the chances of  you slipping down and hurting yourself  but it will also take some of the  pressure off of those elbows thereby  preventing injury further you should  always be engaged always have tension in  the arms this is part of the big benefit  of rope climbing and it'll prevent you  from hurting yourself there are plenty  of variations you can use if you can't  do rope climbs right away some easier  options are just to hold onto the rope  and pull yourself up and down like a  strange pull-up likewise you can use  wall climbs if you can install the rope  somewhere where there's a wall or a tree  trunk and you can kick the legs against  it and scale it like that ninja these  are also great options for mechanical  drop sets do as much rope climbing as  you can and when you can't do anymore  swap to one of these easier variations  as you get really good  and it gets too easy for you then you  can introduce a weighted vest and this  really increases the challenge what I've  been doing lately and yeah I've seen  crazy benefits from rope climbing it's  really changed my physique especially as  I haven't been out to get to the gym as  much lately  I haven't be able to rely on some of my  old favorites like heavy benchpress as  much so I hope you found this video  useful let me know in the comments down  below if you use rope climbs or what  other unusual training techniques or  tools you using in your training head  over to the website for the full article  and also I'd like to take this  opportunity to announce that I am  working on an e-book a massive ebook is  already 70 thousand words long which is  going to also include a full training  program it's called super functional  training functional training means doing  all the things that your body was  designed to be able to do super  functional training means being able to  do things that you don't need to be able  to do but are awesome and at the same  time it also incorporates brain training  a single program for training your body  and mind and it's all laid out it's all  explained and it also includes  descriptions of all the exercises along  with diet plans recipes and loads and  loads of information so if that sounds  cool then stay tuned I'll be announcing  more about it soon lots of people in  requesting this and that's why I decided  to finally do it it's also why I've been  a bit slow with output on occasion if  you want to be notified about that sign  up to the Facebook page I'll leave the  link in the description down below head  over there and I'll be announcing more  details very soon I'll also be giving  several people a kind of preview copy  for free so they can tell me how they  found it give me any feedback so if you  want to be one of those people head over  there and look out for that post anyways  either way please subscribe to the  channel stay tuned for more content like  this and I'll see you next time thanks a  ton for watching and bye for now

